#!/usr/bin/env node
/**
 * AURA — the camera
 *
 *   - A Camera item in the side menu (above Log out) opens a small floating window with your
 *     camera. Drag it by its top bar, resize it from its corner, minimize it to a small bar.
 *     Its buttons: switch camera, mirror, camera on/off, minimize, close.
 *   - The camera only turns on when you press Camera (or Turn on). Closing the preview, or the
 *     power button, turns it off and lets go of it. A red dot shows whenever it's on.
 *   - Settings > Camera: which camera, mirror the preview, preview size.
 *   - Camera in Recordings (off unless you switch it on): while the camera is on, clips you
 *     record with F9, the AURA Bar or the Clips page show it in a corner you pick.
 *   - Nothing is saved or sent anywhere. The picture only goes into a clip you record yourself.
 *
 * How to use:
 *   1. Put this file in your AURA project folder (the one with package.json).
 *   2. Fully quit AURA.
 *   3. Run:   node aura-camera-setup.cjs
 *
 * What it does:
 *   - creates  src/components/camera.jsx   the camera preview, its settings, the recording corner
 *   - edits    src/App.jsx                  the Camera menu item, Settings > Camera, recordings
 *   - creates  tests/camera.cjs             (only if AURA's checks are installed) checks it
 *
 * Every file it changes is copied to <name>.before-camera.bak first.
 * To put everything back:                 node aura-camera-setup.cjs --undo
 * To preview without changing anything:   node aura-camera-setup.cjs --dry-run
 */
